 "title": "Regulation of PAPS Pathway in bPACy and WT Organisms",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the regulation of the PAPS pathway in two organisms, bPACy and WT. The JUB1-X synTF, a synthetic transcription factor, induces IPTG production and regulates the expression of APSK and ATPS, which are involved in the PAPS pathway. The bPACy organism has a lower adenylate energy charge and a proteome, while the WT organism has a higher abundance than bPACy. The PAPS pathway is also influenced by the cAMP-PKA and cAMP-Cyr1 signaling pathways. The cluster also includes various genes and proteins, such as JUB1, RNAP, and PPK, which are involved in transcription and metabolism.",
